{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UhfRhtyz2rbxdx6PngXuew","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Re-repair 作为 supplementary evidence 而非独立贡献。写法: ''preliminary\n2\t  evidence suggests diagnostic granularity enables targeted re-repair (Section 6.2)''\n3\t  但不列入 core claims。降低 claim 强度为 ''diagnostic information has potential downstream\n4\t  utility''。主线仍是三个 core claims。DeepSeek 结果支持 design space 叙事但需要 hedge language (''in\n5\t  our experimental setting'')。仍投 EMNLP Main，准备 Findings 作 realistic landing。'\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: deepseek-cls-repo-v4\n8\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n9\t  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest data,\n10\t    seed 42. 与 Qwen3 repo-level CLS 对标。\n11\t  expected_results:\n12\t    accuracy: 79.3\n13\t    f1_macro: 73.8\n14\t    f1_fail: 63.5\n15\t    f1_pass: 84.1\n16\t    precision_fail: 72.4\n17\t    recall_fail: 56.4\n18\t    precision_pass: 81.8\n19\t    recall_pass: 86.5\n20\t    unparseable_pct: 1.8\n21\t    majority_baseline: 73.0\n22\t    gap_vs_majority_pp: 6.3\n23\t    total_samples: 9784\n24\t  result_rationale: DeepSeek tokenizer 对 repo-level 长序列处理能力与 Qwen3 不同。CLS 任务本身简单（binary），DeepSeek\n25\t    应能达到合理水平但不如 Qwen3-4B 的 82-83%。原因：(1) DeepSeek base 在 code understanding 上略弱于 Qwen3\n26\t    同规模，(2) repo-level 长上下文中 DeepSeek 的 attention pattern 不同导致 fail recall 偏低，(3)\n27\t    但 format compliance 无问题（CLS 只需输出 pass/fail），unparseable 接近 0。与 Qwen3-4B ckpt-4600\n28\t    的 82.35% 差 ~3pp，符合 median 档 'gap 较小' 预期。\n29\t  tables:\n30\t  - name: 'Table: DeepSeek vs Qwen3 Repo-Level CLS (seed 42)'\n31\t    rows:\n32\t    - model: Qwen3-4B\n33\t      accuracy: 82.35\n34\t      f1_macro: 74.74\n35\t      fail_f1: 60.87\n36\t    - model: Qwen3-8B\n37\t      accuracy: 84.79\n38\t      f1_macro: 81.18\n39\t      fail_f1: 72.93\n40\t    - model: DeepSeek-4B\n41\t      accuracy: 79.3\n42\t      f1_macro: 73.8\n43\t      fail_f1: 63.5\n44\t  figures_description:\n45\t  - Bar chart comparing repo-level CLS accuracy across 3 models (Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B,\n46\t    DeepSeek-4B)\n47\t  analysis: DeepSeek CLS 低于 Qwen3 同规模 ~3pp，但仍高于 majority baseline 6.3pp。说明 CLS formulation\n48\t    在不同 model family 上都可行，但绝对水平有差异。这支持 'design space is model-contingent' 叙事。\n49\t- name: deepseek-cls-repo-s123\n50\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n51\t  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level, seed 123. Multi-seed validation\n52\t    for DeepSeek repo CLS.\n53\t  expected_results:\n54\t    accuracy: 77.1\n55\t    f1_macro: 71.5\n56\t    f1_fail: 60.2\n57\t    f1_pass: 82.8\n58\t    precision_fail: 69.8\n59\t    recall_fail: 53.1\n60\t    precision_pass: 79.9\n61\t    recall_pass: 85.8\n62\t    unparseable_pct: 2.1\n63\t    total_samples: 9784\n64\t  result_rationale: Seed variance 在 DeepSeek repo-level 比 func-level 大（small test\n65\t    set effect + repo-level 难度高）。seed123 比 seed42 低 ~2pp，反映了 median 档 'seed variance\n66\t    大' 的假设。两 seed 均值 ~78.2%，落在 [75,82] 范围内。这种 variance 使得统计显著性主张需要更多 seed 或 bootstrap\n67\t    CI，weakens any strong claim。\n68\t  tables: []\n69\t  figures_description:\n70\t  - 'Seed variance plot: DeepSeek repo-level CLS across seeds with error bars'\n71\t  analysis: 两 seed 差异 2.2pp（79.3 vs 77.1），std ~1.6pp。相比 Qwen3 func-level 的 std 0.96pp，repo-level\n72\t    DeepSeek 的 variance 更大。需 hedge：'results are directionally consistent but seed-to-seed\n73\t    variation at repo-level is non-negligible'。\n74\t- name: deepseek-cwm-repo\n75\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n76\t  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 42. 关键实验：验证\n77\t    CWM unparseable 是否是 Qwen3 tokenizer-specific。\n78\t  expected_results:\n79\t    accuracy: 72.8\n80\t    f1_macro: 62.4\n81\t    f1_fail: 42.1\n82\t    f1_pass: 82.7\n83\t    unparseable_pct: 23.5\n84\t    unparseable_count: 2300\n85\t    parseable_accuracy: 78.6\n86\t    exact_match_rate: 31.2\n87\t    precision_fail: 55.3\n88\t    recall_fail: 33.9\n89\t    precision_pass: 76.8\n90\t    recall_pass: 89.4\n91\t    total_samples: 9784\n92\t    majority_baseline: 73.0\n93\t    gap_vs_majority_pp: -0.2\n94\t  result_rationale: Median 档核心假设：DeepSeek CWM unparseable 15-40%，远低于 Qwen3 的 54-93%。这证明\n95\t    CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。但 23.5% unparseable 仍然\n96\t    non-trivial，导致 overall accuracy 被拉低至 majority baseline 附近。parseable subset 上 accuracy\n97\t    78.6% 说明 CWM 在 DeepSeek 上'可以工作'但 format compliance 仍是瓶颈。gap vs CLS 约 6.5pp（79.3\n98\t    vs 72.8），落在 [0,8] 范围内。这个结果 interpretable（方向明确：CLS > CWM）但 not decisive（gap 可能被\n99\t    unparseable handling 策略影响）。\n100\t  tables:\n101\t  - name: 'Table: CWM Unparseable Rate Comparison'\n102\t    rows:\n103\t    - model: Qwen3-4B func-level\n104\t      unparseable_pct: 0\n105\t      accuracy: 87.51\n106\t    - model: Qwen3-4B repo-level\n107\t      unparseable_pct: 93.0\n108\t      accuracy: 58.04\n109\t    - model: DeepSeek-4B func-level\n110\t      unparseable_pct: 0\n111\t      accuracy: 85.77\n112\t    - model: DeepSeek-4B repo-level\n113\t      unparseable_pct: 23.5\n114\t      accuracy: 72.8\n115\t  figures_description:\n116\t  - 'Stacked bar: parseable vs unparseable breakdown by model×level'\n117\t  - 'Accuracy comparison: overall vs parseable-only, showing format compliance bottleneck'\n118\t  analysis: CWM unparseable 从 Qwen3 的 93% 降至 DeepSeek 的 23.5%（-69.5pp），强力支持 'tokenizer-specific\n119\t    failure' claim。但 23.5% 仍不可忽略，说明 repo-level CWM 固有难度。CLS-CWM gap 6.5pp 在 parseable-only\n120\t    上缩小到 0.7pp，进一步证明差异主要来自 format compliance 而非理解能力。\n121\t- name: deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\n122\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n123\t  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 123.\n124\t  expected_results:\n125\t    accuracy: 69.4\n126\t    f1_macro: 58.9\n127\t    f1_fail: 37.6\n128\t    f1_pass: 80.2\n129\t    unparseable_pct: 28.7\n130\t    unparseable_count: 2808\n131\t    parseable_accuracy: 75.3\n132\t    exact_match_rate: 28.9\n133\t    total_samples: 9784\n134\t  result_rationale: CWM generation 对 seed 更敏感（generation diversity → format compliance\n135\t    variance）。seed123 unparseable 比 seed42 高 5pp（28.7% vs 23.5%），导致 accuracy 再降 3.4pp。这种\n136\t    high variance 是 median 档特征：'结果方向明确但 seed variance 大'。两 seed 均值 accuracy ~71.1%，CLS-CWM\n137\t    gap 均值 ~7.1pp。p-value 对这个 gap 在 2 seeds 下 likely 不显著（n=2 paired），需要更多 seed 或换\n138\t    bootstrap。\n139\t  tables: []\n140\t  figures_description: []\n141\t  analysis: DeepSeek CWM 两 seed 差 3.4pp（72.8 vs 69.4），unparseable 差 5.2pp。variance\n142\t    大于 CLS（2.2pp），符合 generation task 固有 instability。如果取 mean，CLS-CWM gap ~7pp，但 CI\n143\t    很宽。写法需要：'CLS outperforms CWM on DeepSeek by 5-9pp depending on seed, though the\n144\t    gap is smaller than on Qwen3 (19-26pp) and primarily attributable to format compliance'。\n145\t- name: swebench-pertest-data\n146\t  plan_id: swebench-pertest-data\n147\t  description: Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test\n148\t    labels. 500 instances × 16 candidates.\n149\t  expected_results:\n150\t    instances_completed: 467\n151\t    instances_failed_docker: 33\n152\t    total_test_pairs: 74720\n153\t    avg_tests_per_instance: 10.0\n154\t    avg_candidates_per_instance: 16\n155\t    pass_rate_gold: 0.98\n156\t    pass_rate_mutant: 0.52\n157\t    docker_timeout_pct: 4.2\n158\t    wall_clock_hours: 22\n159\t    parallel_containers: 16\n160\t  result_rationale: 500 instances 中约 33 个 Docker 环境构建失败（dependency issues, deprecated\n161\t    packages），这在 SWE-bench 社区经验中正常（~6-7% failure rate）。467 个成功 instance 足以构建 dataset。per-test\n162\t    label extraction 本身是 deterministic（run test, check exit code），无 noise。主要 overhead\n163\t    是 Docker build time 和 test suite execution time，16 parallel containers 下约 22h。\n164\t  tables: []\n165\t  figures_description: []\n166\t  analysis: Data construction step，无 accuracy 结论。467 instances 足以支撑后续 repo-level 训练（已有\n167\t    repo-level-cls-v5 用此数据）。缺失的 33 instances 不影响 representativeness（random failure，非\n168\t    systematic bias）。\n169\t- name: diagnostic-rerepair\n170\t  plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n171\t  description: 'Downstream POC: repair agent with per-test failure predictions vs\n172\t    no info. 200 instances, SWE-agent style.'\n173\t  expected_results:\n174\t    control_resolve_rate: 0.22\n175\t    cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.27\n176\t    oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.32\n177\t    random_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.24\n178\t    delta_cls_vs_control_pp: 5.0\n179\t    delta_oracle_vs_cls_pp: 5.0\n180\t    delta_random_vs_control_pp: 2.0\n181\t    n_instances: 200\n182\t    p_value_cls_vs_control: 0.078\n183\t    ci_95_lower_cls_delta: -0.5\n184\t    ci_95_upper_cls_delta: 10.5\n185\t    prompt_format_1_delta: 7.0\n186\t    prompt_format_2_delta: 3.0\n187\t  result_rationale: Median 档预期 CLS-diagnostic (B) 比 control (A1) 提升 3-8pp，统计显著性边缘。这里取\n188\t    5pp（22% → 27%）。基线 22% resolve rate 合理（SWE-bench 上 open-source agent 通常 20-30%）。Oracle\n189\t    (C) 比 B 高 5pp（27% → 32%），说明 diagnostic info 有 room for improvement 但 CLS predictions\n190\t    已捕捉大部分 signal。Random (D) 也有 2pp 提升（24%），这是 median 档的关键 'dilution' 因素：即使 random\n191\t    test feedback 也有些价值（给 agent 任何额外 context 都有帮助），稀释了 CLS-specific 贡献。p=0.078 边缘不显著（n=200,\n192\t    paired McNemar），CI 包含 0。两种 prompt format 效果不一致（7pp vs 3pp），robustness check 不完全通过。\n193\t  tables:\n194\t  - name: 'Table: Re-repair Resolve Rate by Condition'\n195\t    rows:\n196\t    - condition: A1-control (no diagnostic)\n197\t      resolve_rate: 0.22\n198\t      n: 200\n199\t    - condition: B-CLS diagnostic\n200\t      resolve_rate: 0.27\n201\t      n: 200\n202\t    - condition: C-Oracle diagnostic\n203\t      resolve_rate: 0.32\n204\t      n: 200\n205\t    - condition: D-Random diagnostic\n206\t      resolve_rate: 0.24\n207\t      n: 200\n208\t    caption: Resolve rate (pass@1). p(B>A1)=0.078, McNemar paired test.\n209\t  figures_description:\n210\t  - Bar chart with 4 conditions showing resolve rate + 95% CI error bars\n211\t  - 'Prompt format interaction: 2×4 heatmap showing resolve rate by (format × condition)'\n212\t  analysis: 5pp improvement 在方向上支持 diagnostic utility，但 p=0.078 不满足 conventional significance。Random\n213\t    (D) 的 2pp lift 说明 'any feedback helps' confound 存在。写法：'CLS-guided re-repair shows\n214\t    a trend toward higher resolve rate (+5pp, p=0.078), though the effect does not\n215\t    reach statistical significance at α=0.05 in our 200-instance evaluation. We note\n216\t    that even random test feedback provides marginal benefit (+2pp), suggesting the\n217\t    advantage is partially attributable to providing any per-test context rather than\n218\t    CLS-specific diagnostics.' 这足以回应 'no downstream utility' concern，但不能作为 core claim。\n219\t- name: re-repair-phase1-instruct\n220\t  plan_id: re-repair-phase1-instruct\n221\t  description: Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct, 60 instances, 5 conditions (A1/A2/B/C/D),\n222\t    Docker eval, 2 prompt formats.\n223\t  expected_results:\n224\t    n_instances: 60\n225\t    conditions:\n226\t      A1_minimal:\n227\t        resolve_rate_format1: 0.2\n228\t        resolve_rate_format2: 0.22\n229\t        mean_resolve_rate: 0.21\n230\t      A2_test_names:\n231\t        resolve_rate_format1: 0.23\n232\t        resolve_rate_format2: 0.23\n233\t        mean_resolve_rate: 0.23\n234\t      B_cls_diagnostic:\n235\t        resolve_rate_format1: 0.28\n236\t        resolve_rate_format2: 0.24\n237\t        mean_resolve_rate: 0.26\n238\t      C_oracle_diagnostic:\n239\t        resolve_rate_format1: 0.33\n240\t        resolve_rate_format2: 0.3\n241\t        mean_resolve_rate: 0.315\n242\t      D_random_diagnostic:\n243\t        resolve_rate_format1: 0.25\n244\t        resolve_rate_format2: 0.22\n245\t        mean_resolve_rate: 0.235\n246\t    delta_B_vs_A1_pp: 5.0\n247\t    delta_C_vs_B_pp: 5.5\n248\t    delta_B_vs_D_pp: 2.5\n249\t    delta_A2_vs_A1_pp: 2.0\n250\t    p_value_B_vs_A1: 0.092\n251\t    p_value_C_vs_A1: 0.018\n252\t    robustness_format1_passes: true\n253\t    robustness_format2_passes: false\n254\t    pass_at_5:\n255\t      A1: 0.35\n256\t      B: 0.42\n257\t      C: 0.48\n258\t      D: 0.37\n259\t  result_rationale: 60 instances 比 200 instances 方案更现实但 power 更低。Median 档核心特征：(1)\n260\t    B vs A1 +5pp 但 p=0.092（n=60 太小，McNemar power 不足），(2) C vs A1 +10.5pp 显著（p=0.018），证明\n261\t    oracle diagnostic 有 clear value，(3) B vs D 仅 +2.5pp，CLS-specific contribution\n262\t    被稀释，(4) Format 1 效果明显（B=28%）但 Format 2 退化（B=24%），robustness 不通过。A2（test names\n263\t    only）比 A1 高 2pp 说明即使只给 test name 也有些帮助，进一步稀释了 per-test pass/fail prediction 的\n264\t    exclusive contribution。pass@5 差距更大（A1:35% vs B:42%），suggestion that diagnostic\n265\t    info helps exploration diversity。\n266\t  tables:\n267\t  - name: 'Table: Re-repair Phase 1 Results (Qwen3-8B-Instruct, N=60)'\n268\t    rows:\n269\t    - condition: A1-minimal\n270\t      format1: 0.2\n271\t      format2: 0.22\n272\t      mean: 0.21\n273\t    - condition: A2-test-names\n274\t      format1: 0.23\n275\t      format2: 0.23\n276\t      mean: 0.23\n277\t    - condition: B-CLS-diag\n278\t      format1: 0.28\n279\t      format2: 0.24\n280\t      mean: 0.26\n281\t    - condition: C-Oracle-diag\n282\t      format1: 0.33\n283\t      format2: 0.3\n284\t      mean: 0.315\n285\t    - condition: D-Random-diag\n286\t      format1: 0.25\n287\t      format2: 0.22\n288\t      mean: 0.235\n289\t  - name: 'Table: Statistical Tests'\n290\t    rows:\n291\t    - comparison: B vs A1\n292\t      delta_pp: 5.0\n293\t      p_value: 0.092\n294\t      significant: no (α=0.05)\n295\t    - comparison: C vs A1\n296\t      delta_pp: 10.5\n297\t      p_value: 0.018\n298\t      significant: 'yes'\n299\t    - comparison: B vs D\n300\t      delta_pp: 2.5\n301\t      p_value: 0.34\n302\t      significant: 'no'\n303\t    - comparison: C vs B\n304\t      delta_pp: 5.5\n305\t      p_value: 0.065\n306\t      significant: no (marginal)\n307\t  figures_description:\n308\t  - 'Ladder plot: 5 conditions ranked by mean resolve rate with bootstrap CIs'\n309\t  - 'Format robustness: paired difference (Format1 - Format2) per condition, showing\n310\t    B is format-sensitive'\n311\t  - 'Instance-level scatter: per-instance resolve outcome (binary) across conditions,\n312\t    highlighting ''swing'' instances where diagnostic flips result'\n313\t  analysis: Oracle (C) 显著优于 control 证明 per-test diagnostic information 有 intrinsic\n314\t    value for re-repair。但 CLS (B) 与 control 的差异不够显著（p=0.092），且 B vs D 差异更小（p=0.34），意味着\n315\t    CLS prediction quality（87.5% accuracy）不足以完全 unlock 这个 value — 当 CLS 预测错误时反而 misleads\n316\t    agent。写法建议：'Oracle-guided re-repair significantly outperforms the control (p=0.018),\n317\t    establishing that per-test diagnostic information has downstream utility. CLS-guided\n318\t    re-repair shows a positive trend (+5pp) but does not reach significance, suggesting\n319\t    that prediction accuracy is a bottleneck for realizing the full potential of diagnostic-guided\n320\t    repair.' 这 honestly frames the limitation while still demonstrating the concept。\n321\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9e6c9eb-3130-432d-b41b-742928284f63","uuid":"419cc723-b7b2-4657-835b-84f5b310cb06","timestamp":"2026-05-17T04:07:13.641Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T034206/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Re-repair 作为 supplementary evidence 而非独立贡献。写法: ''preliminary\n  evidence suggests diagnostic granularity enables targeted re-repair (Section 6.2)''\n  但不列入 core claims。降低 claim 强度为 ''diagnostic information has potential downstream\n  utility''。主线仍是三个 core claims。DeepSeek 结果支持 design space 叙事但需要 hedge language (''in\n  our experimental setting'')。仍投 EMNLP Main，准备 Findings 作 realistic landing。'\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: deepseek-cls-repo-v4\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest data,\n    seed 42. 与 Qwen3 repo-level CLS 对标。\n  expected_results:\n    accuracy: 79.3\n    f1_macro: 73.8\n    f1_fail: 63.5\n    f1_pass: 84.1\n    precision_fail: 72.4\n    recall_fail: 56.4\n    precision_pass: 81.8\n    recall_pass: 86.5\n    unparseable_pct: 1.8\n    majority_baseline: 73.0\n    gap_vs_majority_pp: 6.3\n    total_samples: 9784\n  result_rationale: DeepSeek tokenizer 对 repo-level 长序列处理能力与 Qwen3 不同。CLS 任务本身简单（binary），DeepSeek\n    应能达到合理水平但不如 Qwen3-4B 的 82-83%。原因：(1) DeepSeek base 在 code understanding 上略弱于 Qwen3\n    同规模，(2) repo-level 长上下文中 DeepSeek 的 attention pattern 不同导致 fail recall 偏低，(3)\n    但 format compliance 无问题（CLS 只需输出 pass/fail），unparseable 接近 0。与 Qwen3-4B ckpt-4600\n    的 82.35% 差 ~3pp，符合 median 档 'gap 较小' 预期。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DeepSeek vs Qwen3 Repo-Level CLS (seed 42)'\n    rows:\n    - model: Qwen3-4B\n      accuracy: 82.35\n      f1_macro: 74.74\n      fail_f1: 60.87\n    - model: Qwen3-8B\n      accuracy: 84.79\n      f1_macro: 81.18\n      fail_f1: 72.93\n    - model: DeepSeek-4B\n      accuracy: 79.3\n      f1_macro: 73.8\n      fail_f1: 63.5\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart comparing repo-level CLS accuracy across 3 models (Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B,\n    DeepSeek-4B)\n  analysis: DeepSeek CLS 低于 Qwen3 同规模 ~3pp，但仍高于 majority baseline 6.3pp。说明 CLS formulation\n    在不同 model family 上都可行，但绝对水平有差异。这支持 'design space is model-contingent' 叙事。\n- name: deepseek-cls-repo-s123\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level, seed 123. Multi-seed validation\n    for DeepSeek repo CLS.\n  expected_results:\n    accuracy: 77.1\n    f1_macro: 71.5\n    f1_fail: 60.2\n    f1_pass: 82.8\n    precision_fail: 69.8\n    recall_fail: 53.1\n    precision_pass: 79.9\n    recall_pass: 85.8\n    unparseable_pct: 2.1\n    total_samples: 9784\n  result_rationale: Seed variance 在 DeepSeek repo-level 比 func-level 大（small test\n    set effect + repo-level 难度高）。seed123 比 seed42 低 ~2pp，反映了 median 档 'seed variance\n    大' 的假设。两 seed 均值 ~78.2%，落在 [75,82] 范围内。这种 variance 使得统计显著性主张需要更多 seed 或 bootstrap\n    CI，weakens any strong claim。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Seed variance plot: DeepSeek repo-level CLS across seeds with error bars'\n  analysis: 两 seed 差异 2.2pp（79.3 vs 77.1），std ~1.6pp。相比 Qwen3 func-level 的 std 0.96pp，repo-level\n    DeepSeek 的 variance 更大。需 hedge：'results are directionally consistent but seed-to-seed\n    variation at repo-level is non-negligible'。\n- name: deepseek-cwm-repo\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 42. 关键实验：验证\n    CWM unparseable 是否是 Qwen3 tokenizer-specific。\n  expected_results:\n    accuracy: 72.8\n    f1_macro: 62.4\n    f1_fail: 42.1\n    f1_pass: 82.7\n    unparseable_pct: 23.5\n    unparseable_count: 2300\n    parseable_accuracy: 78.6\n    exact_match_rate: 31.2\n    precision_fail: 55.3\n    recall_fail: 33.9\n    precision_pass: 76.8\n    recall_pass: 89.4\n    total_samples: 9784\n    majority_baseline: 73.0\n    gap_vs_majority_pp: -0.2\n  result_rationale: Median 档核心假设：DeepSeek CWM unparseable 15-40%，远低于 Qwen3 的 54-93%。这证明\n    CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。但 23.5% unparseable 仍然\n    non-trivial，导致 overall accuracy 被拉低至 majority baseline 附近。parseable subset 上 accuracy\n    78.6% 说明 CWM 在 DeepSeek 上'可以工作'但 format compliance 仍是瓶颈。gap vs CLS 约 6.5pp（79.3\n    vs 72.8），落在 [0,8] 范围内。这个结果 interpretable（方向明确：CLS > CWM）但 not decisive（gap 可能被\n    unparseable handling 策略影响）。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: CWM Unparseable Rate Comparison'\n    rows:\n    - model: Qwen3-4B func-level\n      unparseable_pct: 0\n      accuracy: 87.51\n    - model: Qwen3-4B repo-level\n      unparseable_pct: 93.0\n      accuracy: 58.04\n    - model: DeepSeek-4B func-level\n      unparseable_pct: 0\n      accuracy: 85.77\n    - model: DeepSeek-4B repo-level\n      unparseable_pct: 23.5\n      accuracy: 72.8\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar: parseable vs unparseable breakdown by model×level'\n  - 'Accuracy comparison: overall vs parseable-only, showing format compliance bottleneck'\n  analysis: CWM unparseable 从 Qwen3 的 93% 降至 DeepSeek 的 23.5%（-69.5pp），强力支持 'tokenizer-specific\n    failure' claim。但 23.5% 仍不可忽略，说明 repo-level CWM 固有难度。CLS-CWM gap 6.5pp 在 parseable-only\n    上缩小到 0.7pp，进一步证明差异主要来自 format compliance 而非理解能力。\n- name: deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 123.\n  expected_results:\n    accuracy: 69.4\n    f1_macro: 58.9\n    f1_fail: 37.6\n    f1_pass: 80.2\n    unparseable_pct: 28.7\n    unparseable_count: 2808\n    parseable_accuracy: 75.3\n    exact_match_rate: 28.9\n    total_samples: 9784\n  result_rationale: CWM generation 对 seed 更敏感（generation diversity → format compliance\n    variance）。seed123 unparseable 比 seed42 高 5pp（28.7% vs 23.5%），导致 accuracy 再降 3.4pp。这种\n    high variance 是 median 档特征：'结果方向明确但 seed variance 大'。两 seed 均值 accuracy ~71.1%，CLS-CWM\n    gap 均值 ~7.1pp。p-value 对这个 gap 在 2 seeds 下 likely 不显著（n=2 paired），需要更多 seed 或换\n    bootstrap。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: DeepSeek CWM 两 seed 差 3.4pp（72.8 vs 69.4），unparseable 差 5.2pp。variance\n    大于 CLS（2.2pp），符合 generation task 固有 instability。如果取 mean，CLS-CWM gap ~7pp，但 CI\n    很宽。写法需要：'CLS outperforms CWM on DeepSeek by 5-9pp depending on seed, though the\n    gap is smaller than on Qwen3 (19-26pp) and primarily attributable to format compliance'。\n- name: swebench-pertest-data\n  plan_id: swebench-pertest-data\n  description: Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test\n    labels. 500 instances × 16 candidates.\n  expected_results:\n    instances_completed: 467\n    instances_failed_docker: 33\n    total_test_pairs: 74720\n    avg_tests_per_instance: 10.0\n    avg_candidates_per_instance: 16\n    pass_rate_gold: 0.98\n    pass_rate_mutant: 0.52\n    docker_timeout_pct: 4.2\n    wall_clock_hours: 22\n    parallel_containers: 16\n  result_rationale: 500 instances 中约 33 个 Docker 环境构建失败（dependency issues, deprecated\n    packages），这在 SWE-bench 社区经验中正常（~6-7% failure rate）。467 个成功 instance 足以构建 dataset。per-test\n    label extraction 本身是 deterministic（run test, check exit code），无 noise。主要 overhead\n    是 Docker build time 和 test suite execution time，16 parallel containers 下约 22h。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Data construction step，无 accuracy 结论。467 instances 足以支撑后续 repo-level 训练（已有\n    repo-level-cls-v5 用此数据）。缺失的 33 instances 不影响 representativeness（random failure，非\n    systematic bias）。\n- name: diagnostic-rerepair\n  plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n  description: 'Downstream POC: repair agent with per-test failure predictions vs\n    no info. 200 instances, SWE-agent style.'\n  expected_results:\n    control_resolve_rate: 0.22\n    cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.27\n    oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.32\n    random_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 0.24\n    delta_cls_vs_control_pp: 5.0\n    delta_oracle_vs_cls_pp: 5.0\n    delta_random_vs_control_pp: 2.0\n    n_instances: 200\n    p_value_cls_vs_control: 0.078\n    ci_95_lower_cls_delta: -0.5\n    ci_95_upper_cls_delta: 10.5\n    prompt_format_1_delta: 7.0\n    prompt_format_2_delta: 3.0\n  result_rationale: Median 档预期 CLS-diagnostic (B) 比 control (A1) 提升 3-8pp，统计显著性边缘。这里取\n    5pp（22% → 27%）。基线 22% resolve rate 合理（SWE-bench 上 open-source agent 通常 20-30%）。Oracle\n    (C) 比 B 高 5pp（27% → 32%），说明 diagnostic info 有 room for improvement 但 CLS predictions\n    已捕捉大部分 signal。Random (D) 也有 2pp 提升（24%），这是 median 档的关键 'dilution' 因素：即使 random\n    test feedback 也有些价值（给 agent 任何额外 context 都有帮助），稀释了 CLS-specific 贡献。p=0.078 边缘不显著（n=200,\n    paired McNemar），CI 包含 0。两种 prompt format 效果不一致（7pp vs 3pp），robustness check 不完全通过。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Re-repair Resolve Rate by Condition'\n    rows:\n    - condition: A1-control (no diagnostic)\n      resolve_rate: 0.22\n      n: 200\n    - condition: B-CLS diagnostic\n      resolve_rate: 0.27\n      n: 200\n    - condition: C-Oracle diagnostic\n      resolve_rate: 0.32\n      n: 200\n    - condition: D-Random diagnostic\n      resolve_rate: 0.24\n      n: 200\n    caption: Resolve rate (pass@1). p(B>A1)=0.078, McNemar paired test.\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart with 4 conditions showing resolve rate + 95% CI error bars\n  - 'Prompt format interaction: 2×4 heatmap showing resolve rate by (format × condition)'\n  analysis: 5pp improvement 在方向上支持 diagnostic utility，但 p=0.078 不满足 conventional significance。Random\n    (D) 的 2pp lift 说明 'any feedback helps' confound 存在。写法：'CLS-guided re-repair shows\n    a trend toward higher resolve rate (+5pp, p=0.078), though the effect does not\n    reach statistical significance at α=0.05 in our 200-instance evaluation. We note\n    that even random test feedback provides marginal benefit (+2pp), suggesting the\n    advantage is partially attributable to providing any per-test context rather than\n    CLS-specific diagnostics.' 这足以回应 'no downstream utility' concern，但不能作为 core claim。\n- name: re-repair-phase1-instruct\n  plan_id: re-repair-phase1-instruct\n  description: Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct, 60 instances, 5 conditions (A1/A2/B/C/D),\n    Docker eval, 2 prompt formats.\n  expected_results:\n    n_instances: 60\n    conditions:\n      A1_minimal:\n        resolve_rate_format1: 0.2\n        resolve_rate_format2: 0.22\n        mean_resolve_rate: 0.21\n      A2_test_names:\n        resolve_rate_format1: 0.23\n        resolve_rate_format2: 0.23\n        mean_resolve_rate: 0.23\n      B_cls_diagnostic:\n        resolve_rate_format1: 0.28\n        resolve_rate_format2: 0.24\n        mean_resolve_rate: 0.26\n      C_oracle_diagnostic:\n        resolve_rate_format1: 0.33\n        resolve_rate_format2: 0.3\n        mean_resolve_rate: 0.315\n      D_random_diagnostic:\n        resolve_rate_format1: 0.25\n        resolve_rate_format2: 0.22\n        mean_resolve_rate: 0.235\n    delta_B_vs_A1_pp: 5.0\n    delta_C_vs_B_pp: 5.5\n    delta_B_vs_D_pp: 2.5\n    delta_A2_vs_A1_pp: 2.0\n    p_value_B_vs_A1: 0.092\n    p_value_C_vs_A1: 0.018\n    robustness_format1_passes: true\n    robustness_format2_passes: false\n    pass_at_5:\n      A1: 0.35\n      B: 0.42\n      C: 0.48\n      D: 0.37\n  result_rationale: 60 instances 比 200 instances 方案更现实但 power 更低。Median 档核心特征：(1)\n    B vs A1 +5pp 但 p=0.092（n=60 太小，McNemar power 不足），(2) C vs A1 +10.5pp 显著（p=0.018），证明\n    oracle diagnostic 有 clear value，(3) B vs D 仅 +2.5pp，CLS-specific contribution\n    被稀释，(4) Format 1 效果明显（B=28%）但 Format 2 退化（B=24%），robustness 不通过。A2（test names\n    only）比 A1 高 2pp 说明即使只给 test name 也有些帮助，进一步稀释了 per-test pass/fail prediction 的\n    exclusive contribution。pass@5 差距更大（A1:35% vs B:42%），suggestion that diagnostic\n    info helps exploration diversity。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Re-repair Phase 1 Results (Qwen3-8B-Instruct, N=60)'\n    rows:\n    - condition: A1-minimal\n      format1: 0.2\n      format2: 0.22\n      mean: 0.21\n    - condition: A2-test-names\n      format1: 0.23\n      format2: 0.23\n      mean: 0.23\n    - condition: B-CLS-diag\n      format1: 0.28\n      format2: 0.24\n      mean: 0.26\n    - condition: C-Oracle-diag\n      format1: 0.33\n      format2: 0.3\n      mean: 0.315\n    - condition: D-Random-diag\n      format1: 0.25\n      format2: 0.22\n      mean: 0.235\n  - name: 'Table: Statistical Tests'\n    rows:\n    - comparison: B vs A1\n      delta_pp: 5.0\n      p_value: 0.092\n      significant: no (α=0.05)\n    - comparison: C vs A1\n      delta_pp: 10.5\n      p_value: 0.018\n      significant: 'yes'\n    - comparison: B vs D\n      delta_pp: 2.5\n      p_value: 0.34\n      significant: 'no'\n    - comparison: C vs B\n      delta_pp: 5.5\n      p_value: 0.065\n      significant: no (marginal)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Ladder plot: 5 conditions ranked by mean resolve rate with bootstrap CIs'\n  - 'Format robustness: paired difference (Format1 - Format2) per condition, showing\n    B is format-sensitive'\n  - 'Instance-level scatter: per-instance resolve outcome (binary) across conditions,\n    highlighting ''swing'' instances where diagnostic flips result'\n  analysis: Oracle (C) 显著优于 control 证明 per-test diagnostic information 有 intrinsic\n    value for re-repair。但 CLS (B) 与 control 的差异不够显著（p=0.092），且 B vs D 差异更小（p=0.34），意味着\n    CLS prediction quality（87.5% accuracy）不足以完全 unlock 这个 value — 当 CLS 预测错误时反而 misleads\n    agent。写法建议：'Oracle-guided re-repair significantly outperforms the control (p=0.018),\n    establishing that per-test diagnostic information has downstream utility. CLS-guided\n    re-repair shows a positive trend (+5pp) but does not reach significance, suggesting\n    that prediction accuracy is a bottleneck for realizing the full potential of diagnostic-guided\n    repair.' 这 honestly frames the limitation while still demonstrating the concept。\n","numLines":321,"startLine":1,"totalLines":321}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013zMgH7z5kiwni5sprG8wQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read the paper and the review context. Now I need to conduct a full review with the dream-review-full dispatch template:\n- R1: Method + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n- Full roundtable: Step 1 (independent) → Step 2 (cross-share) → Step 3 (converge) → Step 4 (synthesize)\n\nLet me dispatch both reviewers in parallel, then conduct the roundtable. Let me launch R1 and R2 as parallel agents.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The dream-review-full process requires:\n\n\n1. Two independent reviewers (R1 and R2)\n2. A roundtable process\n\nI should launch R1 and R2 in parallel as agents, get their independent reviews, then conduct the roundtable myself to synthesize. Now I need to draft detailed prompts for both reviewers based on the paper details: \"The Formulation Design Space for Execution-Free Code Verification\" which compares CLS, CWM, and TRAJ formulations across two model families (Qwen3, DeepSeek-R1) at function-level and repo-level complexity.\n\nThe key findings show formulation equivalence at the function level but model-dependent divergence at repo-level—particularly CWM's 93% unparseability on Qwen3 versus 23.5% on DeepSeek—while CLS offers diagnostic granularity at lower cost. The re-repair experiment serves as supplementary evidence rather than a core claim, and I need to emphasize the three main claims with appropriate hedging around the DeepSeek results given statistical significance concerns. The paper is 8 pages submitted to a top ML venue anonymously.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24611,"cache_read_input_tokens":24908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24611},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9e6c9eb-3130-432d-b41b-742928284f63","uuid":"43f16bdd-209a-4a6e-a8c7-3fd15f3cf3c8"}
